Chris Scheers wrote:
<snip>
> The standard failure for the RD53 is an inability to come to speed.  It 
> will spin up and 10 to 30 seconds later, spin down again.  Sometimes it 
> will keep doing this over and over, sometimes it just does it once and 
> then stays spun down.
> 
<snip>

I understood that this failure to load the heads was typically caused by 
a rubber "landing pad" used to give a soft landing to the heads when 
being retracted. The rubber(y) pad gradually goes gooey, and the heads 
"stick" in it. The head motor doesn't have enough power to "unstick" them.

I've seen several web pages with "fixes", ranging from whacking the 
drive with a hammer in the right spot at the right time (low rate of 
success!) to opening up the disk cavity and replacing the pad.

Wilber


