Not sure whether you got a reply on this request :-)
IIRC the system may be configured to remember the default boot device.
On a microVAX 2000 the TEST commands handle that, T 51 , T 52 and T 53.
You might try them on your system. If one of them returns an answer
with a device name then that's the one. The other return a digit, in
the range 0 .. 3 I think. They control the boot process: HALT, BOOT the
default device and what to do after a system failure.
