Howard S Shubs <howard@shubs.net> writes:

> Or maybe I should just try to find a fairly recent SCSI adapter for 
> drives which have been made in the last 5 or 8 years?

You can use wide drives with a HSD05 or HSD10. The trick is to use a
wide shelf, and put a terminator on the A port of the IO module. Some
drives won't play with a narrow controller even when fully terminated.
Doing the term on A port gives you a fully terminated SCSI shelf on
all 16 bits.

