There's no interlock, it's just the issue of getting a cable that has 
that notch.  For the larger systems, like the 3000-500, the thicker 
cables will heat less than the thinner ones.  You can put the notch in a 
standard workstation cable, but you're going to have to decide if the 
thinner cable heats up too much for your safety.  The part number for 
the one in my hand is 17-00083-43.  The certification label on the cable 
says it's 13A, 1625W , 125V but the label on my cable is wrapped back 
over itself so I can't tell if wire guage is listed.  I'm pretty sure 
that I can see molded into the cable 16/3, so I'd guess it's got three 
16ga wires...  This one is a straight at the wall plug but right angle 
at the system end.  IIRC those aren't the easiest to use with the 
DEC3000-500 but you can make it work.

bob



