 Well, RD53's and RD54's were Maxtor drives and, like Zane, I do not
particularly love these devices. The only dead disk in my collection is
an RD54...
Admittedly, I haven't touched a microVAX II in ten years, so I can't
recall off hand whether it understands the command >>> SHOW DEVICE
The microVAX 2000 used something like >>> T 50
If your ultrix tape does not understand the disk it is still possible
that it had no support for your configuration. I'm no ultrix guru but
ra disk references seem to point to RA class disks (like the RA60,
RA82, RA70 or RA91 to name a few). The RD5x drives are no SDI devices
so I'd guess that they'd have different names (rd or rq, with unix who
can guess, right?).
Suggestion: your tape drive seems to work well. Would it be possible to
boot a VMS standalone backup tape (any VMS version from V4.6 upwards
will do nicely)? Standalone backup scans your system and reports the
devices it is seeing.
You did not mention this but did you try to boot from all the disks:
>>> B DUA1 etc?

Hans



