H Vlems wrote:
>  Well, RD53's and RD54's were Maxtor drives and, like Zane, I do not
> particularly love these devices. The only dead disk in my collection is
> an RD54...

Actually, only the RD54 is a Maxtor drive.  It is an unmodified XT2190.

The RD53 is a Micropolis 1325D.  It is a 1325 with a small modification 
to the logic board.

The standard failure for the RD53 is an inability to come to speed.  It 
will spin up and 10 to 30 seconds later, spin down again.  Sometimes it 
will keep doing this over and over, sometimes it just does it once and 
then stays spun down.

You need to listen carefully to the RD53.  It should spin up and in 
about 10 to 20 seconds, you should hear the heads load.  If the heads 
load, it should keep spinning and be OK.

If it spins back down, it needs to be repaired.  I think they replace a 
bearing in the drive.

Even if the drive is OK, if it is not DUA0 or if it does not have a 
bootable system on it, it will not boot.

Booting a stand alone backup (SABACKUP) tape is a good idea.

Good luck!

