GM:

It depends entirely on what OS you're using and how you choose to boot 
the system.
SRM is *EXTREMELY* fussy about video cards whereas AlphaBios is not 
quite so fussy.
That said, if you're going to continue using Win2k Server RC1 or switch 
to Linux then pretty much any PCI style graphics card will do, as long 
as you can find suitable drivers for it.
If you plan to use SRM then you're limited to a small handful of cards. 
Elsa Gloria Synergy (8mb), Diamond Fire Pro GL1000 (with Permedia 2 
chipset), Powerstorm 4D10T, Powerstorm 3D30 or Powerstorm 4D20 are the 
ones that come to mind.  There might be a few others.

Good luck!

TomC


